{#
  The career band at the top of the CV.

  One block per role, positioned along a shared time axis - a flattened
  cousin of the life-in-weeks grid: same idea of giving a span of years a
  shape you can take in at a glance, with one block per job instead of one
  box per week.

  Each block links to that role's heading further down the page, so the band
  doubles as a contents list. Blocks are sized by how long the job lasted, so
  the narrow ones cannot hold a label; every block carries its full details in
  `title` (which works with no JavaScript) and in data attributes that
  assets/ext/js/cv.js reads to fill the caption line below the band.

  Geometry comes from src/_data/career.js - see careerRoles.yml for the dates.
#}
<figure class="career" aria-labelledby="career-caption">
    <div class="career-track">
        {%- for role in career.roles %}
        <a class="career-block{% if role.uncertainEnd %} is-uncertain{% endif %}{% if role.ongoing %} is-current{% endif %}"
           href="#{{ role.id }}"
           style="left: {{ role.left }}%; width: {{ role.width }}%"
           title="{{ role.employer }} — {{ role.title }} ({{ role.from }} to {{ role.to }}, {{ role.duration }})"
           data-employer="{{ role.employer }}"
           data-title="{{ role.title }}"
           data-span="{{ role.from }} to {{ role.to }} &middot; {{ role.duration }}">
            {%- if role.showLabel %}
            <span class="career-block-label">{{ role.employer }}</span>
            {%- endif %}
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="career-axis" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- for tick in career.ticks %}
        <span class="career-tick" style="left: {{ tick.left }}%">{{ tick.year }}</span>
        {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    {#- The resting text is the summary; cv.js swaps in a role's details on
        hover or focus and puts this back on the way out. -#}
    <figcaption id="career-caption" class="career-caption"
                data-default="{{ career.roles | size }} roles &middot; {{ career.startYear }}&ndash;{{ career.endYear }} &middot; {{ career.years }} years">
        {{ career.roles | size }} roles &middot; {{ career.startYear }}&ndash;{{ career.endYear }} &middot; {{ career.years }} years
    </figcaption>
</figure>
